THIS DIRECTORY IS NOT COVERED BY THE AGPL.

The GNU AGPL v3.0 in /LICENSE covers the project's SOURCE CODE. It does not
cover the curated data. This file exists because that boundary is easy to miss
when you are looking at a directory full of .sql files: the schema migrations
here are source code, the seeded property values are not, and they sit side by
side.

WHAT IS SOURCE CODE (AGPL v3.0)
    db/migrations/*.sql     schema structure -- tables, constraints, triggers
    db/tests/*.sql          constraint checks
    db/run.sh, db/test.sh   tooling

WHAT IS PROPRIETARY DATA (all rights reserved)
    db/seeds/*.sql          curated property values, sources, citations,
                            taxonomy content and coverage data
    curation/*.csv          the curation working set, including the extracted
                            Hansen solvent and correlation tables
    any export, dump, fixture or derivative of the above

A seed file that contains BOTH structure and data is proprietary in whole.
Split it before treating any part of it as source.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT A WRITTEN LICENCE
    - copy, redistribute or publish the data, in whole or in substantial part
    - extract a substantial part of it into another database or product
    - use it to train, fine-tune or ground a machine-learning model or
      retrieval system (see docs/legal/ai-usage-policy.md)
    - present it, or figures derived from it, as your own dataset

Individual factual values are not themselves copyrightable in most
jurisdictions. This reservation is over the curated COMPILATION -- the
selection, verification, citation and arrangement of those values, which is
where the work went and where the rights subsist. Where the EU database right
(Directive 96/9/EC) applies, extraction of a substantial part is separately
prohibited regardless of the factual nature of the contents.

